; gevrek's display manager under SELinux.
;
; The system's policy has a domain for display managers (xdm_t): what
; runs in it may check a password, open a session for a person and start
; that session under the person's own label. A program gets into that
; domain by the label of its file. This module gives gevrek-dm that
; label, and the places it keeps things the labels a display manager's
; have, so that it runs as one and not as a service nobody confines
; (unconfined_service_t), whose label the whole session would keep.
;
; Installed with `semodule -i gevrek-dm.cil` and `restorecon` on the
; files (scripts/install-dm.sh does both where SELinux is on).

(filecon "/usr/bin/gevrek-dm" file (system_u object_r xdm_exec_t ((s0) (s0))))
(filecon "/usr/local/bin/gevrek-dm" file (system_u object_r xdm_exec_t ((s0) (s0))))
(filecon "/var/lib/gevrek-greeter(/.*)?" any (system_u object_r xdm_var_lib_t ((s0) (s0))))
(filecon "/run/gevrek-dm(/.*)?" any (system_u object_r xdm_var_run_t ((s0) (s0))))
